# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the LRU cache library.
#
# The library deliberately allocates a small number of process-lifetime objects
# and never frees them. That is a correctness requirement, not an oversight: a
# read_handle may outlive the cache that issued it (the documented
# shutdown_and_wait() path gives up waiting, warns, and destroys the cache
# anyway), and it dereferences the handle-release notifier to test
# `cache_alive` without touching cache-owned memory. Freeing the notifier at
# cache destruction would make that test dangle. The per-shard hazptr/EBR
# domains follow the same policy for the same reason.
#
# LeakSanitizer cannot see that intent — once the cache is gone the notifier is
# unreachable — so these allocations are listed here. Keep this file in sync
# with the `deliberately NEVER freed` sites in the headers; anything else that
# shows up as a leak is a real bug and must not be added.
#
# Format: leak:<substring of the demangled allocating function name>.

leak:init_production_features
